title: ShivPrasad_Day1
tags: 
position: -7,-175
---
<<PlayBackgroundMusic Light_3>>
<<SetBGSprite HutInterior>>

The evening air carries the sounds of children playing in the lanes. Raju chooses to return home instead of joining them. His father will be back from work soon.

The modest home feels charged with anticipation. Raju waits for his father's return, his cricket bat resting beside him. The familiar sounds of Shiv's footsteps create excitement and anxiety in equal measure.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
Shiv Prasad: Raju, where were you this afternoon?

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
Shiv Prasad: Your mother mentioned you were at the ground again instead of with your books.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: I was practicing cricket, Baba. Just for a little while.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: Ramu bhaiya has been teaching me proper technique. I'm getting much better!

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Skeptical">>
Shiv Prasad: Cricket technique? And what about your mathematics technique?

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
Shiv Prasad: Your school test is next week. Will these cricket shots help you solve equations?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: But Baba, I am good at cricket. Really good.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: Even the older boys say so. Maybe this could be something more than just playing.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
Shiv Prasad: Talent? Beta, I've seen talented boys before.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
Shiv Prasad: Talented at cricket, talented at singing, talented at painting.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
Shiv Prasad: Do you know where most of them are now?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Quizzical">>
Raju: Where are they?

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
Shiv Prasad: Working in the same factories as me, or worse.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Disappointed">>
Shiv Prasad: Unemployed and dependent on their families.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
Shiv Prasad: Talent doesn't pay the bills. Education does.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
Shiv Prasad: A government job does. Skills that employers value do.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Sad">>
Raju: So I should just give up something I love?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Disappointed">>
Raju: Something I might be good at?

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
Shiv Prasad: I'm not asking you to give up joy, beta.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
Shiv Prasad: I'm asking you to be realistic about priorities.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
Shiv Prasad: Study first. Secure your future first.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
Shiv Prasad: Then, if there's time and energy left, play your cricket.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
Shiv Prasad: But never let it become more important than your education.

<<HideAllCharacters>>
As evening settles, Shiv's practical wisdom hangs heavy in the air. Raju understands the tension between dreams and security. His father's words carry genuine concern, yet they feel like barriers around what makes him feel most alive.

<<set $ShivPrasad_Day = 2>>
<<EndEvent true>>
===

title: ShivPrasad_Day2
tags: 
position: -75,-229
---
<<PlayBackgroundMusic Light_3>>
<<SetBGSprite HutInterior>>

Despite yesterday's difficult conversation, Raju stays home this evening. He sits in their small courtyard, practicing his cricket grip with an old bat.

Raju positions himself where his father will see him. His movements show dedication and a calculated attempt to prove his commitment. He waits for Shiv to return from work.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Skeptical">>
Shiv Prasad: Again with that bat in your hands? Beta, don't you ever rest?

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Disappointed">>
Shiv Prasad: I thought we discussed this yesterday.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: I do rest, Baba. But when I hold this bat...

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: When I practice, when I play... I don't feel tired.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: I feel alive. Like I could be someone special.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Proud">>
Raju: Someone who makes you proud.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Worried">>
Shiv Prasad: Alive? Special? These are dangerous words!

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
Shiv Prasad: Dreams like these have destroyed families.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Angry">>
Shiv Prasad: I've watched fathers waste their savings on cricket fantasies.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Disappointed">>
Shiv Prasad: Only to end up in debt and despair.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
Shiv Prasad: Food puts life in your body, not cricket!

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
Shiv Prasad: Steady work makes you special in society, not games!

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: Then let me work hard at cricket, Baba.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: The same way you work hard at the factory.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: Give me one chance to prove I can do both.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Confident">>
Raju: Studies and cricket. Let me show you they can coexist.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Skeptical">>
Shiv Prasad: Words are easy to speak, beta.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Skeptical">>
Shiv Prasad: Promises are easy when your belly is full.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
Shiv Prasad: But proving balance between dreams and duty?

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
Shiv Prasad: That's harder than any factory shift I've worked.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
Shiv Prasad: That requires maturity most adults don't possess.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: I don't know if I can, Baba. But I want to try.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: I want to try so badly it hurts when I think about giving up.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Quizzical">>
Shiv Prasad: If you're serious about this balance...

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
Shiv Prasad: If you truly believe you can handle both, then show me.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
Shiv Prasad: Don't tell me - show me.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
Shiv Prasad: Prove your cricket makes you a better student.

<<HideAllCharacters>>
Shiv's challenge hangs in the air like a bridge between doubt and possibility. Raju recognizes his father has offered something precious - a genuine opportunity. The weight of expectation settles on his young shoulders.

<<set $ShivPrasad_Day = 3>>
<<EndEvent true>>
===

title: ShivPrasad_Day3
tags: 
position: -75,-229
---
<<PlayBackgroundMusic Light_3>>
<<SetBGSprite HutInterior>>

After two intense days, Raju approaches his father directly after dinner. Yesterday's discussion opened a small door of possibility.

The quiet intimacy of their evening meal creates the perfect atmosphere. Raju senses this will be pivotal. The flickering oil lamp casts dancing shadows as father and son prepare to negotiate the terms of a test.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
Shiv Prasad: Raju, come sit with me.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
Shiv Prasad: For two days you've told me you can handle both cricket and studies.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
Shiv Prasad: But words and promises are easy when there's no real test.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: I meant everything I said, Baba.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Confident">>
Raju: I really can do both. Just give me a chance to prove it.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
Shiv Prasad: That's exactly what I'm going to do.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
Shiv Prasad: Your mathematics test is in seven days.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
Shiv Prasad: I want you to score well on that exam. Not just pass, but score well.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Anxious">>
Raju: Seven days? Baba... I haven't been studying as much as I should.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Worried">>
Raju: Math is hard for me. What if seven days isn't enough time?

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
Shiv Prasad: Then you'll learn something important about managing priorities.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
Shiv Prasad: If cricket has left you unprepared, you've answered the question yourself.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
Shiv Prasad: Here's my offer. Score well on that mathematics test.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
Shiv Prasad: I mean really well, better than you've ever done before.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
Shiv Prasad: And I'll not only support your cricket, I'll help you pursue it properly.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Anxious">>
Raju: And if I don't do well?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Worried">>
Raju: What if I study as hard as I can but still struggle?

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
Shiv Prasad: Then we'll know you're not ready for this balance.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
Shiv Prasad: Excellence requires sacrifice, beta.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
Shiv Prasad: If you can't sacrifice cricket time to excel at studies, you don't understand commitment.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
Shiv Prasad: This isn't a game, Raju.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
Shiv Prasad: If you fail this test, if cricket proves more important than education...

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
Shiv Prasad: We end this conversation permanently.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
Shiv Prasad: No more negotiations, no more chances.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: I understand, Baba. I won't let you down.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Confident">>
Raju: Seven days from now, you'll see I can be serious about both.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Quizzical">>
Raju: How should I approach these seven days, Baba?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Anxious">>
Raju: What's the best way to prove I can handle both?

<<AutoAdvance true>>
Make a Choice
<<AutoAdvance false>>
-> Raju: I'll focus completely on studies. Cricket can wait.
    <<jump ShivPrasad_Day3a>>
-> Raju: I'll use cricket discipline to improve my studying.
    <<jump ShivPrasad_Day3b>>
-> Raju: I'll let cricket passion energize all my efforts.
    <<jump ShivPrasad_Day3c>>
===

title: ShivPrasad_Day3a
tags:
position: -308,129
---
<<set $ShivPrasad_Path = "a">>

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: I'll prove myself by focusing completely on studies, Baba.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: Let me show you academics can be my priority.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: I'll reduce cricket time dramatically and put everything into mathematics.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
Shiv Prasad: That's a significant sacrifice, beta.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
Shiv Prasad: But be careful - I want genuine understanding, not desperate cramming.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
Shiv Prasad: Show me disciplined studying, not panic.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: I understand, Baba.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: I'll create a proper study schedule and stick to it religiously.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: Cricket can wait - my education comes first, just like you've said.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Smiling">>
Shiv Prasad: Your willingness to sacrifice shows maturity.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Smiling">>
Shiv Prasad: But remember - this isn't about giving up cricket forever.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Smiling">>
Shiv Prasad: It's about proving you understand priorities.

<<HideAllCharacters>>
Raju's dramatic reduction in cricket shows maturity that impresses Shiv. The sacrifice represents more than test prep - it tests character. His choice reflects understanding that responsibility sometimes requires temporary sacrifice of joy.

<<set $ShivPrasad_Day = 4>>
<<EndEvent true>>
===

title: ShivPrasad_Day3b
tags:
position: -55,122
---
<<set $ShivPrasad_Path = "b">>

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: I'll show you cricket discipline actually helps my studies, Baba.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Confident">>
Raju: Watch me use both together.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Determined">>
Raju: Let me prove they support each other instead of competing.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Skeptical">>
Shiv Prasad: You think cricket and studies can actually work together?

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Quizzical">>
Shiv Prasad: That's a bold claim, beta.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Skeptical">>
Shiv Prasad: Show me exactly how this supposed synergy works.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: Cricket taught me about consistent daily practice.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Confident">>
Raju: Breaking complex skills into manageable parts.

